478→\label{fig:memory_comparison}
479→\end{figure}
480→
481→\subsection{Weight-Tying Correctness}
482→
483→The weight-tying fix is critical for model correctness. Without it, models with \texttt{tie\_word\_embeddings=True} produce gibberish output due to uninitialized \texttt{lm\_head} weights. Since all three evaluated models (Qwen3-0.6B, Llama-3.2-1B, and Llama-3.2-3B) use weight tying, this fix is essential for correct operation. We verified correctness by comparing outputs of single-node inference (with full loading) against multi-node inference (with selective loading and weight-tying restoration), confirming identical token sequences for the same prompt and sampling parameters.
484→
485→\subsection{Comparison with Related Systems}
486→
