\subsection{Selective Loading Impact}

Selective loading provides significant benefits across all model sizes (Table~\ref{tab:loading_perf}):
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Load time:} Up to $5.2\times$ reduction for WORKER shards, with benefits scaling consistently across model sizes (4.8$\times$ for 0.6B, 5.2$\times$ for 1B, 4.4$\times$ for 3B).
    \item \textbf{Peak memory:} 62--81\% reduction across all configurations, critical for memory-constrained devices.
    \item \textbf{Scalability:} For Llama-3.2-3B, selective loading reduces peak memory from 52.6\,MB to 11.4--19.8\,MB per node, enabling inference on devices that cannot hold the full model.
\end{itemize}

